// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
pragma hyperion >=0.0.1;

/**
 * Leg B's principal, as the objection chamber of decision D6 reads it
 * (design §6.8). Implemented by the Ark Staking bond (`ArkCatBondStore` or a
 * view beside it); declared here so the governor compiles without it.
 *
 * WHY PRINCIPAL AND NOT veARK
 * ---------------------------
 * veARK receives no cash flow from Ark Staking (D8), yet it prices cover and
 * sets indemnity — decisions that move value between the two legs. The chamber
 * gives the leg that bears the decision a way to force a stricter re-vote. It
 * is escalation, not a veto: a Contested proposal can still pass, at 15% quorum
 * and 75% approval.
 *
 * CHECKPOINTING RULE THE IMPLEMENTER MUST KEEP
 * --------------------------------------------
 * `principalAt(holder, epoch)` is the principal `holder` held at the boundary
 * that OPENED `epoch` — never a live balance. The governor asks at the epoch in
 * which the proposal was queued, so principal subscribed after a proposal became
 * visible in the timelock cannot object to it, and a transfer during the
 * objection window cannot count the same principal twice.
 * `totalPrincipalAt(epoch)` is the sum of the same quantity over all holders.
 */
interface IObjectionSource {
    function principalAt(address holder, uint256 epoch) external view returns (uint256);

    function totalPrincipalAt(uint256 epoch) external view returns (uint256);
}
